    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-australian-energy-regulator-separation-act-2025-sch-2-sec-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 Enterprise Agreement",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-australian-energy-regulator-separation-act-2025#sch-2-sec-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-australian-energy-regulator-separation-act-2025.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-australian-energy-regulator-separation-act-2025.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe ACCC Enterprise Agreement:\n(a) continues, on and from the commencement day, to cover and\napply to APS employees:\n(i) who it covered and applied to immediately before the\ncommencement day; and\n(ii) who, on the commencement day, are members of the\nstaff of the AER; and\n(b) covers and applies to APS employees who are at the\nclassification levels covered by the ACCC Enterprise\nAgreement whose employment as a member of the staff of\nthe AER commences on or after the commencement day.\n(2)\nOn and after the commencement day, the ACCC Enterprise Agreement\ncovers and applies to the AER Chair as the Agency Head of the APS\nemployees who are members of the staff of the AER.\n(3)\nThis item does not prevent the variation or termination of the ACCC\nEnterprise Agreement in accordance with law.\n(4)\nThis item does not prevent the terms and conditions of employment of\nAPS employees who are members of the staff of the AER from being\nvaried on or after the commencement day:\n(a) in accordance with those terms and conditions; or\n(b) by or under a law.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions  Schedule 2\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions  Part 2\nNo. 59, 2025\nCompetition and Consumer Amendment (Australian Energy Regulator\nSeparation) Act 2025\n(5)\nThis item does not affect the operation of section 58 of the Fair Work\nAct 2009.\nNote:\nSection 58 of that Act deals with the interaction between one or more enterprise\nagreements.",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThe ACCC Enterprise Agreement:\n(a) continues, on and from the commencement day, to cover and\napply to APS employees:\n(i) who it covered and applied to immediately before the\ncommencement day; and\n(ii) who, on the commencement day, are members of the\nstaff of the AER; and\n(b) covers and applies to APS employees who are at the\nclassification levels covered by the ACCC Enterprise\nAgreement whose employment as a member of the staff of\nthe AER commences on or after the commencement day.\n(2)\nOn and after the commencement day, the ACCC Enterprise Agreement\ncovers and applies to the AER Chair as the Agency Head of the APS\nemployees who are members of the staff of the AER.\n(3)\nThis item does not prevent the variation or termination of the ACCC\nEnterprise Agreement in accordance with law.\n(4)\nThis item does not prevent the terms and conditions of employment of\nAPS employees who are members of the staff of the AER from being\nvaried on or after the commencement day:\n(a) in accordance with those terms and conditions; or\n(b) by or under a law.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions  Schedule 2\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions  Part 2\nNo. 59, 2025\nCompetition and Consumer Amendment (Australian Energy Regulator\nSeparation) Act 2025\n(5)\nThis item does not affect the operation of section 58 of the Fair Work\nAct 2009.\nNote:\nSection 58 of that Act deals with the interaction between one or more enterprise\nagreements.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-australian-energy-regulator-separation-act-2025-sch-2-sec-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-australian-energy-regulator-separation-act-2025-sch-2-sec-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "785c024f560c392a28c80e669f21caad8da1e9d6baf3774802e98b82d2d36da2",
      "skos:note": "Continues to cover and apply to APS employees"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-australian-energy-regulator-separation-act-2025#sch-2-sec-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 Enterprise Agreement",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe ACCC Enterprise Agreement:\n(a) continues, on and from the commencement day, to cover and\napply to APS employees:\n(i) who it covered and applied to immediately before the\ncommencement day; and\n(ii) who, on the commencement day, are members of the\nstaff of the AER; and\n(b) covers and applies to APS employees who are at the\nclassification levels covered by the ACCC Enterprise\nAgreement whose employment as a member of the staff of\nthe AER commences on or after the commencement day.\n(2)\nOn and after the commencement day, the ACCC Enterprise Agreement\ncovers and applies to the AER Chair as the Agency Head of the APS\nemployees who are members of the staff of the AER.\n(3)\nThis item does not prevent the variation or termination of the ACCC\nEnterprise Agreement in accordance with law.\n(4)\nThis item does not prevent the terms and conditions of employment of\nAPS employees who are members of the staff of the AER from being\nvaried on or after the commencement day:\n(a) in accordance with those terms and conditions; or\n(b) by or under a law.\n\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions  Schedule 2\nApplication, saving and transitional provisions  Part 2\nNo. 59, 2025\nCompetition and Consumer Amendment (Australian Energy Regulator\nSeparation) Act 2025\n(5)\nThis item does not affect the operation of section 58 of the Fair Work\nAct 2009.\nNote:\nSection 58 of that Act deals with the interaction between one or more enterprise\nagreements."
    },
    {
