    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-australian-energy-regulator-separation-act-2025-sch-2-sec-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6 References in Enterprise Agreement",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-australian-energy-regulator-separation-act-2025#sch-2-sec-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-australian-energy-regulator-separation-act-2025.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-australian-energy-regulator-separation-act-2025.pdf, p.17",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nOn and from the commencement day, the ACCC Enterprise Agreement\nhas effect in relation to the AER as if:\n(a) a reference to the Chairperson were a reference to the AER\nChair; and\n(b) a reference to the Australian Competition and Consumer\nCommission, or the ACCC, were a reference to the AER.\n(2)\nTo avoid doubt, this item does not prevent the ACCC Enterprise\nAgreement from being varied or terminated on or after the\ncommencement day.\n\nSchedule 2  Application, saving and transitional provisions",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nOn and from the commencement day, the ACCC Enterprise Agreement\nhas effect in relation to the AER as if:\n(a) a reference to the Chairperson were a reference to the AER\nChair; and\n(b) a reference to the Australian Competition and Consumer\nCommission, or the ACCC, were a reference to the AER.\n(2)\nTo avoid doubt, this item does not prevent the ACCC Enterprise\nAgreement from being varied or terminated on or after the\ncommencement day.\n\nSchedule 2  Application, saving and transitional provisions",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-australian-energy-regulator-separation-act-2025-sch-2-sec-6-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "65310703d382d866fd30823cc81f4ad5c6e92ea7f91029d1182e41de4ca23c42",
      "skos:note": "References in Enterprise Agreement"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-australian-energy-regulator-separation-act-2025#sch-2-sec-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6 References in Enterprise Agreement",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 17,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nOn and from the commencement day, the ACCC Enterprise Agreement\nhas effect in relation to the AER as if:\n(a) a reference to the Chairperson were a reference to the AER\nChair; and\n(b) a reference to the Australian Competition and Consumer\nCommission, or the ACCC, were a reference to the AER.\n(2)\nTo avoid doubt, this item does not prevent the ACCC Enterprise\nAgreement from being varied or terminated on or after the\ncommencement day.\n\nSchedule 2  Application, saving and transitional provisions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-australian-energy-regulator-separation-act-2025-sch-2-sec-6-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
